  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the skewness of the two lotteries, with a preference for more right-skewed (i.e., worse outcomes having higher probability) distributions. However, the individual does not discuss or consider the shape of the outcome distributions, symmetry, or skewness. They do not compare the two lotteries structurally. Instead, they focus only on Lottery B, describing its 50% chance as a coin flip and expressing emotional concern about the large loss, while noting the possibility of avoiding loss. There is no indication that they assessed which lottery has more probability on worse outcomes or used any concept related to skewness. The information considered (emotional reaction, binary uncertainty) does not align with the information required by the decision reason (distribution shape, skew). The justification is affective and experiential, not structural. Therefore, there is no evidence that the decision reason was used.",
